{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1026083-technocracy-the-shadowlands-and-the-afterlife","id":1026083,"title":"Technocracy, the Shadowlands, and the afterlife","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-03T11:42:22-08:00","id":1026083,"title":"Technocracy, the Shadowlands, and the afterlife","content":"A question regarding this came up recently and I realized I didn't actually know the answer. <br /> <br /> What is the Technocracy &quot;party line&quot; concerning the Shadowlands and metaphysical questions of the afterlife?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T12:12:31-08:00","id":1026102,"title":"","content":"I think shodowlands is like other realms and they see it as another dimension. Ghosts are referrd to as PLE's (Post Life Entities). My personal favorite Void Enginer acronym.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T12:13:21-08:00","id":1026103,"title":"","content":"According to Tychoidean cosmology (the Void Engineer model of the cosmos), the Umbrae are generated by the minds of those on Earth. Human minds continue to generate models of objects and people - &quot;ghosts&quot; - after they've been destroyed; the inherent contradiction shunts these phenomena into Entropic Space, which the ancients identified as the underworld. (Void Engineers Rev, pp. 54-56).<br /> <br /> That said, the VE still consider Post-Life Entities (or Entropic Extra-Dimensional Entities) extremely fucking dangerous for all that.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate considers ghosts fiction. The Progenitors consider them psychological- and Paradox-orientated phenomena - though ones that can disrupt equipment. The NWO consider them dangerous within Technocratic installations and a threat to public confidence in hypertech, and best handled by the Void Engineers. Iteration X similarly leave them to the VEs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T12:52:56-08:00","id":1026122,"title":"","content":"In WtO's <i>Doomslayer: Into the Labyrinth</i> the talent Helldiving, used for traveling the Labyrinth, is listed as possessed by &quot;Extremely Foolish Void Engineers&quot;. So some have gone very deep indeed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T13:02:09-08:00","id":1026127,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that is one of the problems that the Mages have, the Dark Umbra is really dangerous territory for them. They are outnumbered thousands to one by Wraiths (if I remember correctly, Wraiths are supposed to have a population of 1:20 in the Shadowlands while Mages are supposed to have a population of 1:100,000 on the Earth) and, while the majority of Wraiths are not inclined to mess with Mages while they are on their side of the Shroud (at least not in the territory controlled by the Dark Kingdom of Iron), I am sure that most Wraiths would be willing to kick the rear end of any uppity Mage that came to their side of the Shroud and did not show them proper respect. I am sure that more than one Void Engineer expedition went down in flames, with everyone dying horribly, because they rubbed the local Wraiths the wrong way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T13:48:36-08:00","id":1026148,"title":"","content":"Somehow I see parts of the Syndicate as having an affinity for Spectres. Considering how mind-numbingly brutal organized crime and the underworld are (even more so when you factor in prostitution, drugs, and especially prisons), Syndics involved in it would encounter Spectres or Wraiths quite often. The &quot;dig your own grave&quot; thing might have even been started/popularized by the Syndicate as a means of creating a Restless soul. Also: &quot;Even if we kill you, you are still indebted to us...&quot; . The new Syndicate Convention Book talks about Enforcers wanting to establish a new Methodology dealing with the criminal underworld; the higher-ups aren't enthusiastic about it.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could have some Syndics with the know-how how to help any Restless they encounter during their job; especially ones that get created due to their actions. (A Syndicate member in a crime family definitely boosts their power - hence more people get caught up in the mafia's grubby hands.) Their foci would be simple - manipulation of Fetters, Haunts, the Shroud, Passions, Angst, Pathos through oratory, giving gifts, doing deals, exchanges, promises etc. Seeing how valuable, scarce and desired those things are in the Shadowlands, I think already back in days of Order of Reason the High Guild might have seen an opportunity for power and profit. Especially since with lots of money and influence you can control how a city develops on a large scale - altering Haunts, changing the flow of Pathos, buying &amp; selling Fetters et al. It would be very Technocratic with how you can influence Wraiths through relatively mundane actions. (Which might get developed into Procedures and Adjustments later.)<br /> <br /> Maybe the High Guild/Syndicate were the ones who got rid of the Deathlords' Fetters? It would possibly be part of Order's of Reason agenda to limit the Restless' influence and capabilities; or perhaps the ghosts were seen as potential allies.<br /> <br /> (Maybe WWI was a Syndicate or Technocracy ploy to cause the 4th Great Maelstorm?! And possibly other Great Maelstorms too had their origin(s) in actions of Technocratic Mages :&gt;.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 01-03-2017, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T15:02:35-08:00","id":1026178,"title":"","content":"One thing that a lot of people are glancing over here. Most people can't see Wraiths unless the Wraith in question wants to be seen.<br /> <br /> In order to even feel the presence of a Wraith, you would need Spirit magic (or Dimensional Science), and the study of Dimensional Science is strictly prohibited to all but the Void Engineers.<br /> This means that, with the exception of the Ghostbusters and some other Void Engineers who take the interest, most Technocrats have probably never heard of the Shadowlands, let alone consider making day-trips. The official party line as mandated by NWO is that they simply don't exist. When you die, that's just it, you're dead.<br /> Individual Technocrats may have other ideas, some may have their own personal religious interpretations of the afterlife, but that's not Science. No self-respecting Technocrat would ever come forward and try to claim their beliefs as fact.<br /> A few of the higher ups in each convention may be aware of Wraiths, or PLEs as the Engineers term them, but it certainly would not be common knowledge. NWO especially would be doing everything in their power to dismiss claims of Ghosts with their own team of &quot;Paranormal Investigators&quot; in order to obfuscate any events, create plausible mundane explanations and deal with any other loose threads. This would be supported by the Syndicate who would use their ties with the media to sensationalise the stories, turning them into outlandish tabloid style &quot;My Sister Married a Zombie&quot; style spectacles, adding fabrication to the events, culminating in books and films which permanently banish these sightings to the realm of fiction.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy as a whole has a lot to lose if the masses every discovered that Death was not the definitive end we always thought it would be. Think of all the lost avenues of control (and revenue) in Life Insurance and Health and Safety control measures, in Healthcare plans (both social and competitive), and in plane out fear.<br /> Any NWO leader aware of the Underworld would never allow it to become common knowledge, and probably have teams in place to deal with any potential leaks, especially from the Void Engineers.<br /> <br /> As for Wraiths trying to contact them, there are a number of factors which would limit their attempts. Firstly the strength of the Shroud/Gauntlet, which tends to be very thick in places where Technocrats usually operate. This would severely hamper their ability to interact. Sure it gets weaker in specific places at certain times of year, but that can very easily be brushed off by the Technocrat as &quot;all in their mind&quot;.<br /> <br /> Even then, Wraiths are fairly limited in how they can interact with either the world of the living or living people by the Arcanoi they possess. Some Arcanoi may allow one to cross the Shroud, and others may allow one to interact with objects like a Poltergeist, control humans like Puppets, or enter their Dreams, but not all Wraiths have access to such powers, and even then it can take many decades of practice before such feats are powerful enough to use consistently. In which time their Fetters may be destroyed, thus permanently exiling them deeper into the underworld.<br /> <br /> And if that wasn't enough to deal with, there's the politics of the underworld to contend with. Charon's Law strictly forbids any kind of interactions with the living. And while little acts of involvement, especially ones which pertain to Passions and Fetters, may be understood by some groups, full scale operations will most likely result in a one way ticket to the soulforges.<br /> <br /> So the way I see it, most Wraiths would have too much to lose by trying to contact Technocratic members (if they are even aware of who the Technocracy are). And most Technocrats wouldn't have the knowledge or clearance to interact with Wraiths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-03-2017, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T22:34:24-08:00","id":1026334,"title":"","content":"Well, that is the case in the territories controlled by the Dark Kingdom of Iron, but the majority of the Shadowlands is not under the control of Stygia. Africa is controlled by the Dark Kingdom of Ivory, East Asia is controlled by the Dark Kingdom of Jade, South Asia is controlled by Swar, etc. The rules can change really quickly when you are traveling across the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T03:30:09-08:00","id":1026436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1026083-technocracy-the-shadowlands-and-the-afterlife?p=1026334#post1026334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that is the case in the territories controlled by the Dark Kingdom of Iron, but the majority of the Shadowlands is not under the control of Stygia. Africa is controlled by the Dark Kingdom of Ivory, East Asia is controlled by the Dark Kingdom of Jade, South Asia is controlled by Swar, etc. The rules can change really quickly when you are traveling across the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>That may be the case, but the basic physics of how Wraiths interact with the Skinlands stay consistent across the world. i.e. The shroud needs to be weak, the Arcanoi need to be apt, and the object will be unable to see, hear, or touch the Wraith without Spirit.<br /> <br /> Also, the Technocracy is primarily based in the West. They like to make a big show on how they are a Global force in the world, but their reach only extends so far outside of the West before other groups start to become more dominant. For example, the Five Metal Dragons of the East have greater dominance in China than the Western Technocracy.<br /> <br /> I don't know if it's ever been stated whether other Technocratic forces have been asserting dominance in places like the Middle East, India, the various countries of Africa and South America, or if it's just been an ongoing battle from the Western Technocracy, but I can imagine if it's happened in the East, it's likely to have happened everywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T04:35:30-08:00","id":1026447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1026083-technocracy-the-shadowlands-and-the-afterlife?p=1026178#post1026178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that a lot of people are glancing over here. Most people can't see Wraiths unless the Wraith in question wants to be seen.<br /> <br /> A few of the higher ups in each convention may be aware of Wraiths, or PLEs as the Engineers term them, but it certainly would not be common knowledge. NWO especially would be doing everything in their power to dismiss claims of Ghosts with their own team of &quot;Paranormal Investigators&quot; in order to obfuscate any events, create plausible mundane explanations and deal with any other loose threads. This would be supported by the Syndicate who would use their ties with the media to sensationalise the stories, turning them into outlandish tabloid style &quot;My Sister Married a Zombie&quot; style spectacles, adding fabrication to the events, culminating in books and films which permanently banish these sightings to the realm of fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect this is dependent on often the Traditions interact with and ally with wraiths. The Technocrats can't control what a Reality Deviant throws in their face. It's all well and good saying ghosts don't exist, but you don't want your agent to freeze up when some asshole hermetic summons up their beloved grandmother. The whole PLEs are projections of memories is innocuous enough to spread among field agents, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T04:50:10-08:00","id":1026450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1026083-technocracy-the-shadowlands-and-the-afterlife?p=1026447#post1026447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suspect this is dependent on often the Traditions interact with and ally with wraiths. The Technocrats can't control what a Reality Deviant throws in their face. It's all well and good saying ghosts don't exist, but you don't want your agent to freeze up when some asshole hermetic summons up their beloved grandmother. The whole PLEs are projections of memories is innocuous enough to spread among field agents, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or you could just say &quot;Don't believe the Reality Deviant's lies&quot;. Whatever they say about it being the ghost of their grandmother is just supersticious rubbish. They are just doing their usual magic show stuff and throwing in a few illusions. Trying to undermine the idea that Death is truly the end.<br /> Anything a Wraith can do can be similar enough as something a Mage could do that the Technocracy at the lower levels wouldn't really distinguish. Reality Deviants be messing with things they don't understand and calling it &quot;magic&quot;. Only the Union is properly equipped to harness and understand these powers. The union says they aren't ghosts, so whatever they are, it's not that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T05:27:43-08:00","id":1026458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1026083-technocracy-the-shadowlands-and-the-afterlife?p=1026450#post1026450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Or you could just say &quot;Don't believe the Reality Deviant's lies&quot;. Whatever they say about it being the ghost of their grandmother is just supersticious rubbish. They are just doing their usual magic show stuff and throwing in a few illusions. Trying to undermine the idea that Death is truly the end.<br /> Anything a Wraith can do can be similar enough as something a Mage could do that the Technocracy at the lower levels wouldn't really distinguish. Reality Deviants be messing with things they don't understand and calling it &quot;magic&quot;. Only the Union is properly equipped to harness and understand these powers. The union says they aren't ghosts, so whatever they are, it's not that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but Reality Deviants messing with things they don't understand implies that the Technocracy does understand and it is useful for it to show that. The Technocracy is capable of saying &quot;It's classified&quot; and &quot;Here's the simple version, there's no room in the budget to teach you more.&quot; While I have no doubt that they pull the former more than they have to, Wraiths are close enough to classical superstition and the projection explanation is so much better than nothing that I think in this case the latter is likely. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T05:38:38-08:00","id":1026461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1026083-technocracy-the-shadowlands-and-the-afterlife?p=1026458#post1026458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but Reality Deviants messing with things they don't understand implies that the Technocracy does understand and it is useful for it to show that. The Technocracy is capable of saying &quot;It's classified&quot; and &quot;Here's the simple version, there's no room in the budget to teach you more.&quot; While I have no doubt that they pull the former more than they have to, Wraiths are close enough to classical superstition and the projection explanation is so much better than nothing that I think in this case the latter is likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I go back to the original point. Without Spirit or Dimensional Science, there is no way you'd know it was a Wraith.<br /> <br /> If there really was a mage that was doing all kinds of stuff with Wraiths, then the higher ups of NWO would just pull their investigators off the case and let the NSC handle it until there was nothing left to question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T06:22:25-08:00","id":1026470,"title":"","content":"I have to add Second Sight, Awareness and Mind and possibly other perks let you at least sense, if not outright see, Wraiths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T06:48:46-08:00","id":1026475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1026083-technocracy-the-shadowlands-and-the-afterlife?p=1026461#post1026461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then I go back to the original point. Without Spirit or Dimensional Science, there is no way you'd know it was a Wraith.<br /> <br /> If there really was a mage that was doing all kinds of stuff with Wraiths, then the higher ups of NWO would just pull their investigators off the case and let the NSC handle it until there was nothing left to question.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem isn't knowing what it is, the problem is knowing what it isn't. If you did have enough Dimensional Science to scan it, you'd already know what a PLE is. When your dear departed grandmother shows up and you know the Reality Deviant she's hanging around isn't scanning your mind or your timeline, that's a problem.<br /> <br /> Hell, just saying &quot;ghosts aren't real, but some of those aliens we let the VEs handle pretend to be them,&quot; lets your field agents not waste their time on a run of the mill haunting. Hacking off the second part strikes me as secrecy solely for the sake of secrecy; great if you need that as a story element, not so good if you don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T07:00:17-08:00","id":1026480,"title":"","content":"Of course, what you do not know can literally kill you. There is nothing preventing a Wraith with Embody 4 from making one of your mortal followers it's Consort, dropping into the Skinlands (invisible to everyone but him but tangible to the physical world) while visiting him and causing physical chaos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T07:02:35-08:00","id":1026481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1026083-technocracy-the-shadowlands-and-the-afterlife?p=1026470#post1026470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to add Second Sight, Awareness and Mind and possibly other perks let you at least sense, if not outright see, Wraiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind wouldn't be enough without knowledge in Spirit unless they were on the same side of the gauntlet as you.<br /> Awareness would probably help you &quot;feel a presence&quot;, but without knoweldge in the spirit sphere, that would be all you get. Also, since most cities are Necropoli of sorts in the Shadowlands, the chances are that any presence felt wouldn't be too much different to the background level of Shadowland wraiths in the area anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1026083-technocracy-the-shadowlands-and-the-afterlife?p=1026475#post1026475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem isn't knowing what it is, the problem is knowing what it isn't. If you did have enough Dimensional Science to scan it, you'd already know what a PLE is. When your dear departed grandmother shows up and you know the Reality Deviant she's hanging around isn't scanning your mind or your timeline, that's a problem.<br /> <br /> Hell, just saying &quot;ghosts aren't real, but some of those aliens we let the VEs handle pretend to be them,&quot; lets your field agents not waste their time on a run of the mill haunting. Hacking off the second part strikes me as secrecy solely for the sake of secrecy; great if you need that as a story element, not so good if you don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it depends on how common such an occurrence is.<br /> <br /> My guess is this probably doesn't actually happen all that often. Most Wraiths don't hang around for long. Either they don't have that many fetters and so transcend almost immediately; or will become enslaved as Thralls and go through an afterlife of servitude at best, and a short trip to the soulforgers. When an infant wraith emerges from the cauls, it could be weeks or months since their original death, by which point they are still not 100% aware of what has happened, let alone ready to use Arcanoi for anything all that useful. So the chances to finding the Wraith that coincides with the correct Technocrat and that they haven't already transcended, fallen to oblivion, have been enslaved, had their fetters broken, or become a brick, are actually pretty low.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T07:35:36-08:00","id":1026509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1026083-technocracy-the-shadowlands-and-the-afterlife?p=1026436#post1026436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That may be the case, but the basic physics of how Wraiths interact with the Skinlands stay consistent across the world. i.e. The shroud needs to be weak, the Arcanoi need to be apt, and the object will be unable to see, hear, or touch the Wraith without Spirit.<br /> <br /> Also, the Technocracy is primarily based in the West. They like to make a big show on how they are a Global force in the world, but their reach only extends so far outside of the West before other groups start to become more dominant. For example, the Five Metal Dragons of the East have greater dominance in China than the Western Technocracy.<br /> <br /> I don't know if it's ever been stated whether other Technocratic forces have been asserting dominance in places like the Middle East, India, the various countries of Africa and South America, or if it's just been an ongoing battle from the Western Technocracy, but I can imagine if it's happened in the East, it's likely to have happened everywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Five Metal Dragons are also a PART of the Technocracy. Ostensibly.<br /> <br /> As for the Middle East, wasn't there an older bit of lore that was basically &quot;All the Iraq/other middle eastern wars done by America were really a cover for the Technocracy trying to kill the Taftani.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which the Taftani won.<br /> <br /> As for ghosts, Ghosts aren't real. Therefor anything claiming to be a ghost is a liar.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy aren't evidence based scientists. that's the Etherites thing. The Technocracy by and large are politicians and Engineers. They don't seek greater truths. They HAVE their truths. Anything that violates those is aberrant and in need of correction or destruction.<br /> <br /> So if a Technocrat sees his dear departed grandma's ghost. Well obviously it's a trick. A lie. And Primally charged bullets hit wraiths just as well as they do anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 01-04-2017, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T07:47:58-08:00","id":1026515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1026083-technocracy-the-shadowlands-and-the-afterlife?p=1026509#post1026509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Five Metal Dragons are also a PART of the Technocracy. Ostensibly.<br /> <br /> As for the Middle East, wasn't there an older bit of lore that was basically &quot;All the Iraq/other middle eastern wars done by America were really a cover for the Technocracy trying to kill the Taftani.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which the Taftani won.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Metal Dragons maybe a part of the Technocracy, but there are ideological differences in they way they handle things, with each head holding slightly different opinions on the role mysticism takes in society, all of which are a far cry away from the centralised &quot;Only Science&quot; approach of the West.<br /> <br /> M20 seems to imply that not only did the taftani win the wars, but they bascially became the head honchos for a lot of the economic gains that the countries within the middle east have been partisan to, Dubai being one of the bigger examples of this. How this ties in to the bigger Technocrat narrative has yet to be revealed though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T08:54:10-08:00","id":1030608,"title":"","content":"<i>The Book of Madness</i> 2nd edition has this written when discussing the possibility of Nephandi drawing their power from the dreams (or nightmares) of the spectral Neverborn. Some Technocrats think that there is a link between Gorool awakening around the time Nephandi were attacked by the Traditions-Technocracy alliance, and the Nephandi being suspiciously weak.<br /> &quot;<i>Even now, a report from a gang of ghostly spies sits on the desk of the Skeletal Lord of the dead. Inside are the details of a proposed invasion of the Labyrinth by a multi-Convention strike force. The assault's stated purpose is simple: To awaken the slumbering Malfeans, thus perilously weakening the resurgent Nephandi. As for the effect that this tactic would have on the Shadowlands, the Technocratic assessment is chillingly simple: unimportant.</i>&quot;<br /> This suggests that Technocracy either has vast resources and Dark Umbra expertise...or they are seriously out of touch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1026083-technocracy-the-shadowlands-and-the-afterlife?p=1026178#post1026178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In order to even feel the presence of a Wraith, you would need Spirit magic (or Dimensional Science), and the study of Dimensional Science is strictly prohibited to all but the Void Engineers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't it that it was prohibited only to Iteration-X by the Computer? And this changed in the post-Reckoning reorganization of the Technoracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 01-12-2017, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T09:59:15-08:00","id":1030633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1026083-technocracy-the-shadowlands-and-the-afterlife?p=1030608#post1030608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't it that it was prohibited only to Iteration-X by the Computer? And this changed in the post-Reckoning reorganization of the Technoracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the books reference study of DS as a specifically VE thing. Most other conventions prefer not to go anywhere near it, especially after the dimensional anomaly. Guide to the Technocracy calls it &quot;The Forbiden Fruit of the Void Engineers&quot;, and M20 says: &quot;Dimensional Science remains largely exclusive to a single Convention: the Void Engineers. In many regards, it\u2019s a well-kept secret, propagated only through intense training at VE facilities.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not a leap to think that study of DS would be actively discouraged outside of the Engineers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T13:46:22-08:00","id":1030763,"title":"","content":"Everyone EXCEPT the Iterators had access to it. Because the only reason the Iterators didn't was the computer being a spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T09:27:51-08:00","id":1031203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1026083-technocracy-the-shadowlands-and-the-afterlife?p=1030633#post1030633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most of the books reference study of DS as a specifically VE thing. Most other conventions prefer not to go anywhere near it, especially after the dimensional anomaly. Guide to the Technocracy calls it &quot;The Forbiden Fruit of the Void Engineers&quot;, and M20 says: &quot;Dimensional Science remains largely exclusive to a single Convention: the Void Engineers. In many regards, it\u2019s a well-kept secret, propagated only through intense training at VE facilities.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not a leap to think that study of DS would be actively discouraged outside of the Engineers.</div> </div> </div> </div>A M20 reference would seem to be the most current authoritative statement to this end. Phrases like &quot;well kept secret&quot; and &quot;propagated only through intense training at VE facilities&quot; would seem to put it on par with Primal Utility as &quot;hands off/proprietary/specific high level clearance needed&quot; learning material.<br /> <br /> Also, notably, phrases NOT in a particular Convention's splat book. So the self-promoting-biad-correction-filter doesn't need to be applied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T11:19:29-08:00","id":1031260,"title":"","content":"Why would the majority of the Technocracy (not including the Five Metal Dragons) need DS? With the exception of the VEs, the majority of the threats that the Technocracy faces are on the Earth (and even the Garou have to come back to the Earth eventually).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T16:59:45-08:00","id":1031381,"title":"","content":"There are EDE's All over earth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","a